course: dictionary
lesson: 6361
title: MRI: a machine that sees inside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: MRI is short for magnetic resonance imaging. It is an abbreviation, so the letters stand for longer words that are hard to say quickly. Say the letters one at a time: em-ar-eye.
explain: «An MRI scanner in hospital uses an extremely strong magnet and radio waves to make pictures of the inside of the body, so metal must stay outside the room.» The clues are magnet, radio waves and pictures of the inside of the body. So an MRI is a machine that takes pictures inside you without cutting you open.
explain: As a noun, an MRI can be the test or the picture it makes. You can «have an MRI», or a doctor can show you the MRI. An MRI scan means the same as an MRI: one test, with its pictures.
fact: MRI stands for magnetic resonance imaging.
fact: An MRI machine uses strong magnets and radio waves, and it uses no harmful radiation.
fact: MRI scans show soft parts of the body, such as the brain, muscles and ligaments, very clearly.
fact: Patients lie still inside a tube, and the machine is very noisy.
fact: Metal must be kept out of the MRI room because the magnet is so powerful.
exercise: «An MRI scanner in hospital uses an extremely strong magnet and radio waves.» What does MRI stand for? | Modern radio installation | *Magnetic resonance imaging | Magnetic rays inside | Medical report and index
exercise: «Metal must stay outside the room.» Why? | Because metal makes the machine quieter | Because metal is too heavy for the floor | *Because the powerful magnet could pull it | Because metal makes the pictures colder
exercise: Tom's doctor says he needs an MRI. What is an MRI? | A pair of special glasses for reading | A tube you sleep in to stop headaches | A kind of X-ray that hurts | *A hospital test that makes detailed pictures inside the body
test: What must a patient do during an MRI scan? | Stand up and walk around | *Lie still inside a tube | Run on a treadmill | Sing as loudly as possible
test: «MRI scans show soft parts clearly, such as the brain and muscles.» What does this tell you about an MRI? | *It shows soft parts of the body in detail | It only shows bones, like an X-ray | It shows the time of day | It shows the weather outside the hospital
exam: Which sentence uses MRI correctly? | *«Mum had an MRI scan on her knee to see what was wrong.» | «Mum had an MRI, which means she was very hungry.» | «Mum had an MRI of the weather outside the hospital.» | «Mum had an MRI and then she was a magnet.»
